.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt HANDLE_REVOKE 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm handle_revoke
.Nd revoke rights from a handle and its descendants
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn handle_revoke h rights_mask
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
removes the rights in
.Fa rights_mask
from the handle
.Fa h
and, transitively, from every handle derived from it by
.Xr handle_dup 2 ,
.Xr handle_transfer 2
or a scheme reply attachment, including handles held by another process.
A mask of zero means every right
.Fa h
currently holds.
The handle remains open with its remaining rights.
.Pp
A right that was revoked returns
.Er EPERM
when a later operation needs it; a right that was never granted returns
.Er EACCES .
Bits not held by
.Fa h
are ignored.
The operation is idempotent; a stale or unknown handle returns
.Er EBADF .
A handle derived after a revoke only receives the remaining rights.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Zero on success; a negative
.Va errno
on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EBADF
.Fa h
is not a live handle.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr handle_dup 2 ,
.Xr handle_transfer 2 ,
.Xr proc_namespace 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1, contract C17.
